<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Evrytania</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Eurytania</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Evrytania is a mountainous regional unit of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pindus">Pindus</a> range, with its capital at Karpenisi. Remote and thinly populated, it was a stronghold of the Greek resistance during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> occupation, and in March 1944 EAM established the Political Committee of National Liberation at the village of Viniani there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/evrytania.jpg" alt="Evrytania" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Evrytania_prefecture,_Greece_-_political_map_-_muncipality_level_-_numbered.svg: Christaras A derivative work: Pitich... · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2010_Dimi_Evrytanias_numbered.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
